course: dictionary
lesson: 9167
title: Snowshoes and the clues around them
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence around it tells you which one. «A snowshoe is a wide flat frame you tie under your boot.» Here snowshoe is a thing you wear. Then you read «To snowshoe means to walk on snow wearing snowshoes», and now snowshoe is an action.
explain: Look for clues like «so it does not sink». The snow leopard's paws work like snowshoes so the animal does not sink into deep snow. From that clue you can guess a snowshoe is wide and helps you stay on top of the snow.
explain: Sometimes a word is used to compare things. «Its wide paws work like snowshoes» tells you the paws do the same job as snowshoes. Check your guess by swapping in your meaning: wide paws that spread weight so they do not sink still makes sense.
fact: A snowshoe is a wide flat frame you tie under your boot.
fact: Snowshoes let you walk on deep snow without sinking.
fact: To snowshoe means to walk on snow wearing snowshoes.
fact: A snowshoe hare is a hare with big furry feet that turns white in winter.
fact: In science, a snowshoe spreads your weight over a bigger area, so the pressure is smaller.
exercise: «A snowshoe is a wide flat frame you tie under your boot.» What is a snowshoe? | A type of sled pulled by dogs | A small boot for summer walks | A furry paw of an animal | *A wide flat frame worn under a boot
exercise: The snow leopard's paws work «like snowshoes so it does not sink». Why does this help the leopard? | It helps the leopard roar loudly | It keeps its tail warm | *It spreads its weight on deep snow | It makes the leopard run faster on grass
exercise: «We went to snowshoe across the frozen lake.» What does snowshoe mean here? | To shout loudly across the lake | *To walk on snow wearing snowshoes | To wrap yourself in a scarf | To swim under the ice
test: Why does a snowshoe help you walk on deep snow? | *Because it spreads your weight so you do not sink | Because it makes you lighter than air | Because it melts the snow under your feet | Because it stops the wind
test: In science, what does a snowshoe do to pressure? | It makes the pressure bigger | It turns the pressure into heat | *It makes the pressure smaller | It makes the pressure disappear
exam: Read «Every cat is built for its own home: the snow leopard's wide paws work like snowshoes on mountain snow.» What do the paws help the snow leopard do? | Roar very loudly | *Walk on mountain snow without sinking | Climb tall trees quickly | Swim across a lake
